{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1193"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/olympics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__olympics.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",518],["-","Harry"],["+","Harry,"],["=",1],["+","who had himself served two tours in Afghanistan with the British Army, "],["=",78],["+","Some games are defined not by ability but by community. "],["=",2],["+","Maccabiah Games, first held in Tel Aviv in 1932 and staged in Israel generally every four years since 1953, usually in the year after the Olympics, bring together Jewish athletes from around the world; with some 9,000 competitors in 2013 they ranked among the largest sporting events on earth, and the IOC has recognised them as a regional sports event since 1961.\n\nThe "],["=",239],["+","\n| Maccabiah Games | Tel Aviv 1932 | Jewish athletes |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",494],["+","der selbst zweimal mit der britischen Armee in Afghanistan im Einsatz gewesen war, "],["=",84],["+","Manche Spiele definiert nicht die Leistungsfähigkeit, sondern die Gemeinschaft. Die Makkabiade, erstmals 1932 in Tel Aviv ausgetragen und seit 1953 in der Regel alle vier Jahre in Israel veranstaltet, meist im Jahr nach den Olympischen Spielen, bringt jüdische Sportler aus aller Welt zusammen; mit rund 9000 Teilnehmern im Jahr 2013 zählte sie zu den größten Sportveranstaltungen der Erde, und seit 1961 erkennt das IOC sie als regionale Sportveranstaltung an.\n\n"],["=",253],["+","\n| Makkabiade | Tel Aviv 1932 | jüdische Sportler |"]]}]},
